VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  Read the checks.  A downward ending would have been the framework's completions showing themselves (universal 1/mu, or
  r_ta ~ M_b^(1/4)); an upward departure would have been LambdaCDM's 2-halo term.  The measured answer is what it is; the
  3-sigma lower bounds in section 3 are the quantity to quote either way, and they are a bound on ANY relativistic
  completion of the framework that ends the boost inside the KiDS reach.

